"Celebrating 50 Years of Earth Science for the Global Community (https://www.iugs.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Anthropocene_short_IUGS-ICS_Statement-1.pdf)\nciteturn15view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn13view1\",\"id\":42}); Total lines: 72\nL0@P0: International Union of Geological Sciences\nL1@P0: \nL2@P0: 20 March 2024\nL3@P0: It is with the delegated authority of the IUGS President and\nL4@P0: Secretary General and on behalf of the International\nL5@P0: Commission on Stratigraphy (ICS) that the vote by the ICS\nL6@P0: Subcommission on Quaternary Stratigraphy (SQS) to reject the\nL7@P0: proposal for an Anthropocene Epoch as a formal unit of the\nL8@P0: Geologic Time Scale is approved. The voting members of SQS\nL9@P0: have extensive experience and wide expertise in Quaternary\nL10@P0: stratigraphy and chronology. Their vote was approved by the\nL11@P0: ICS executive, and that approval was overwhelmingly\nL12@P0: supported by the chairs of the ICS subcommissions. Despite its\nL13@P0: rejection as a formal unit of the Geologic Time Scale,\nL14@P0: Anthropocene will nevertheless continue to be used not only\nL15@P0: by Earth and environmental scientists, but also by social\nL16@P0: scientists, politicians and economists, as well as by the public\nL17@P0: at large. It will remain an invaluable descriptor of human\nL18@P0: impact on the Earth system.\nL19@P0: www.iugs.org\nL20@P0: President\nL21@P0: Prof. John LUDDEN CBE\nL22@P0: The Lyell Centre,\nL23@P0: Heriot-Watt University, Edinburgh\nL24@P0: Edinburgh | EH14 4AP\nL25@P0: United Kingdom\nL26@P0: Tel: +44 (0) 7895 331 504\nL27@P0: Email: J.ludden@hw.ac.uk\nL28@P0: Secretary General\nL29@P0: Prof. Stanley C. FINNEY\nL30@P0: Department of Geological Sciences\nL31@P0: California State University - Long Beach\nL32@P0: Long Beach, CA 90840\nL33@P0: USA\nL34@P0: Email: Stan.Finney@csulb.edu\nL35@P0: Treasurer\nL36@P0: Prof. Hiroshi